    "film": {
      "chunk_bytes": 16777216,
      "poll_interval_s": 30,
      "poll_max_s": 1800,
      "chunk_timeout_s": 300
    },
    "evidence": {
      "reels": "confirmed: developers.facebook.com/docs/video-api/guides/reels-publishing (read 2026-11-17): POST {page}/video_reels upload_phase=start, binary POST to the returned rupload address (headers offset and file_size), GET {video}?fields=status until video_status is ready, POST {page}/video_reels upload_phase=finish with video_state DRAFT, SCHEDULED or PUBLISHED. What a DRAFT is, and whether and how a draft can be published later, is NOT documented there: the first controlled draft test shows it.",
      "film": "partly confirmed: developers.facebook.com/docs/video-api/guides/publishing (read 2026-11-17): Resumable Upload API (POST {app}/uploads, POST upload:<id> with file_offset, GET upload:<id> to resume) gives a file handle; POST graph-video.facebook.com/{page}/videos with fbuploader_video_file_chunk=<handle>; published and unpublished_content_type (DRAFT) are parameters of the Page videos reference. Not exercised against Meta with a system-user token yet.",
      "cover": "documented, not yet exercised: POST {video}/thumbnails with source (an image file, at most 10 MB) and is_preferred=true, a Page token, permissions pages_read_user_content, pages_manage_engagement and pages_show_list (developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video/thumbnails, read 2026-11-17); the Reels guide links to it as 'Add a custom cover photo for your reel'. Meta says nothing about Reels, drafts or processing state there, and says a thumbnail cannot be updated or deleted through the API, so it is posted once per file. GET {video}/thumbnails (pages_read_engagement) works on a Reel draft (confirmed live).",
      "limits": "confirmed live 2026-11-17 (GET /me?fields=video_upload_limits with the system-user token): length 14460 seconds, size 28633115306 bytes. The app reads the limits again before every film upload."
    },
    "cover": {
      "required_permissions": [
        "pages_read_user_content",
        "pages_manage_engagement",
        "pages_show_list"
      ],
      "max_mb": 10,
      "source": "https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video/thumbnails/ (read 2026-11-17: POST /{video}/thumbnails takes `source` and `is_preferred`, at most 10 MB; the page does not mention Reels, so it is tested live)"
    }
